## Program Outcome

Tool Shed preserves HPT2 and completed ledgers as immutable historical evidence while all new work
uses generic identities and read-only validation. Performance and CI qualification operate on
stable declared inputs, and migration, upgrade, rollback, deployment, release, and reconciliation
prove the boundary without losing history.

## M1-HISTORICAL-BOUNDARY-FROZEN — Baseline, HPT2 fixture, and terminal ledgers

Status: complete
Evidence: baseline commit `02703bf`; implementation commit `a72662f`; EVD-0073; CAMP-0123 terminal and reconciled

Outcome: Freeze the accepted starting state, isolate HPT2 compatibility from live bootstrap state,
and enforce append-only historical-ledger behavior.

Gates:

- `G1-BASELINE-AND-CANDIDATE-BOUNDARY`: the existing validation-timing candidate is dispositioned;
  exact source commit `02703bf`, database revision/checkpoint 437, and passing 388-test release
  validation form the clean baseline; later planning and validation do not rewrite ledgers merely
  to establish a starting state.
- `G2-HPT2-COMPATIBILITY-FIXTURE-FROZEN`: one compact checked-in fixture preserves every accepted
  HPT2 UUID and relationship, callers select it explicitly, and unrelated live records cannot
  expand it or request another fixed ID.
- `G3-TERMINAL-LEDGER-IMMUTABILITY`: ordinary updates to reconciled terminal ledgers fail precisely;
  explicit append-only correction and supersession retain original and later provenance.

Candidate campaign: `freeze-hpt2-compatibility-and-terminal-ledgers`.

## M2-GENERIC-READ-ONLY-VALIDATION — New identities and non-mutating checks

Status: complete
Evidence: implementation commit `a72662f`; EVD-0074; CAMP-0124 terminal and reconciled

Depends on: M1.

Outcome: Route every new entry point through generic identity allocation and make validation
observational rather than state-changing.

Gate:

- `G4-GENERIC-IDENTITY-AND-READ-ONLY-VALIDATION`: new Idea, map, roadmap, milestone, campaign, and
  direct-work cycles allocate generic managed IDs without HPT2 registry growth; functional
  validation leaves Git status, SQLite revision, tracked checkpoint, and lifecycle views unchanged.

Candidate campaign: `generalize-outcome-identities-and-make-validation-read-only`.

## M3-STABLE-PERFORMANCE-CI — Deterministic performance and risk-matched routing

Status: complete
Evidence: implementation commit `a72662f`; EVD-0075; CAMP-0125 terminal and reconciled

Depends on: M2.

Outcome: Qualify performance against a frozen production-shaped corpus and route CI from declared
changed surfaces while preserving override and scheduled coverage.

Gate:

- `G5-STABLE-PERFORMANCE-AND-CI-POLICY`: the frozen benchmark and relative regression policy are
  repeatable; live timing is advisory with a runaway ceiling; path classes select the documented
  minimum profile; explicit overrides and scheduled full cross-platform validation catch routing
  mistakes.

Candidate campaign: `stabilize-performance-fixtures-and-change-aware-ci`.

## M4-UPGRADE-RELEASE-RECONCILED — Migration, rollout, and closed loop

Status: complete
Evidence: EVD-0076; EVD-0077; released `v0.38.0`; exact-SHA Linux/Windows CI, installed-skill synchronization, released-client upgrade/rollback, production verification, and upward reconciliation passed

Depends on: M3.

Outcome: Prove no-loss migration and rollback, qualify the maintainer and disconnected-client
upgrade paths, deploy and verify the configured work environment, then complete release provenance
and reconcile every accepted requirement and material change.

